From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:27:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] media: iris: treat a coded size beyond the decoder's
 limits as unset

Chromium sets the OUTPUT (bitstream) format of a stateful V4L2 decoder
before it knows the stream's size; the Chromium 126 in the Steam client
asks for 2048x2048. iris keeps that size in fmt_src, and at REQBUFS
iris_check_session_supported() counts it against the platform's frame
limit. On AR50_LITE (QCM2290, SM6115), whose limit is 8160 macroblocks
(1920x1088), 2048x2048 is 16384, so every session is refused:

  qcom-iris 5a00000.video-codec: current session not supported(-12)

and Chromium never uses the hardware decoder.

The coded size of the OUTPUT format is optional: the decoder learns the
real one from the bitstream, and iris already replaces an unset (0x0)
size with a placeholder. Treat a size beyond the frame limits the same
way. A size within them is still checked as before, so a stream that
states a size the hardware cannot decode (1920x1200 on AR50_LITE, which
the gen1 firmware crashes on) is still refused at REQBUFS.

Tested on a MANGMI Air X (SM6115) with Steam's own startup_machine.webm
(1080p VP9) in the Steam client: Chromium now picks V4L2VideoDecoder.

Signed-off-by: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
index 7f89e745a4b1..9357ac1894aa 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
@@ -196,6 +196,7 @@ int iris_vdec_try_fmt(struct iris_inst *inst, struct v4l2_format *f)
 
 int iris_vdec_s_fmt(struct iris_inst *inst, struct v4l2_format *f)
 {
+	struct platform_inst_caps *caps = inst->core->iris_platform_data->inst_caps;
 	struct v4l2_format *fmt, *output_fmt;
 	struct vb2_queue *q;
 	u32 codec_align;
@@ -206,9 +207,14 @@ int iris_vdec_s_fmt(struct iris_inst *inst, struct v4l2_format *f)
 		return -EBUSY;
 
 	/* Width and height are optional, so fall back to a valid placeholder
-	 * resolution until the real one is decoded from the bitstream.
+	 * resolution until the real one is decoded from the bitstream. A coded
+	 * size beyond the frame limits is a client's upper bound, not the
+	 * stream's (Chromium asks for 2048x2048): treat it as unset too.
 	 */
-	if (f->fmt.pix_mp.width == 0 && f->fmt.pix_mp.height == 0) {
+	if ((f->fmt.pix_mp.width == 0 && f->fmt.pix_mp.height == 0) ||
+	    (V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(f->type) &&
+	     (f->fmt.pix_mp.width > caps->max_frame_width ||
+	      f->fmt.pix_mp.height > caps->max_frame_height))) {
 		f->fmt.pix_mp.width = DEFAULT_WIDTH;
 		f->fmt.pix_mp.height = DEFAULT_HEIGHT;
 	}
